flowchart TB
    accTitle: Current webhook delivery architecture
    accDescr: Ingestion buffers events on an event bus. Processing acknowledges on receipt, uses a synchronous request-response enrichment call as an assumption, waits for both datastore and search-index write acknowledgments as an assumption, then hands results to delivery. The two writes are assumed non-atomic. Failed delivery returns to the event bus and repeats processing. Dashboard and API reads are assumed independent of delivery; a visible record does not prove successful delivery. Customer endpoints are outside platform control. A separate assumed outcome-update path feeds customer-visible status, but its durability is unspecified.
    apps[Customer applications] --> gateway[API gateway: authentication and tenant rate limits]
    gateway --> ingestion[Ingestion: validate events]
    ingestion --> bus[(Event bus)]
    bus --> processing[Processing: acknowledge on receipt]
    processing <-->|Assumption: synchronous request-response| enrichment[Enrichment service]
    processing <-->|Assumption: wait for both write acknowledgments| data[(Datastore and search index)]
    processing -->|After enrichment and both writes| delivery[Delivery service]
    data -->|Assumption: independent reads| dashboard[Dashboard and API]
    delivery -->|Webhook attempt| endpoints[Customer webhook endpoints: outside platform control]
    endpoints -.->|Response, or timeout with unknown outcome| delivery
    delivery -.->|Assumption: separate status update, durability unspecified| data
    delivery -.->|Failed attempt: reprocess event| bus
